 *
 * for example "MATH | Calculus | 100 | 31". Fields may be padded with spaces, so every
 * field must be trimmed before use. Department and course are text; level and students
 * are whole numbers. Rows are always well formed and the list itself is never null.
 *
 * Complete both methods:
 *
 *  - byDepartmentAndLevel returns a TreeMap from department to a TreeMap from level to the
 *    TOTAL number of students in that department at that level. Two rows with the same
 *    department and level add together, even if they are different courses.
 *
 *      {"MATH | Calculus | 100 | 31", "MATH | Logic | 100 | 9", "ART | Clay | 200 | 12"}
 *      -> {ART={200=12}, MATH={100=40}}
 *
 *  - coursesByDepartment returns a TreeMap from department to the DISTINCT course names in
 *    that department, sorted alphabetically. A course listed twice appears once.
 *
 *      -> {ART=[Clay], MATH=[Calculus, Logic]}
 *
 * Both methods return an empty TreeMap for an empty input list -- never null. Because the
 * maps are TreeMaps, printing them shows the keys in sorted order, which is what the tests
 * rely on.
 */
